  "summary": "An explainer on Flock Safety's ALPR and PTZ cameras, describing how the nationwide network works, why activists and some cities are vandalizing or deactivating them, and concerns about tracking, ICE-related searches, and false matches. Names cities that have canceled contracts and cites a wrongful-stop incident in Plymouth, Minnesota.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "City governments have joined in by deactivating the cameras or canceling contracts with Flock in Fort Collins, Colorado; Eugene, Oregon; Madison, Wisconsin; Knoxville, Tennessee; Syracuse, New York; and Walla Walla, Washington.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "despite Flock not sharing data with agencies like U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement, police officers have been performing searches to aid in immigration sweeps",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Flock camera saw my entire plate, but it still flagged it as a match",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    }
  ],
